<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Penang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Penang is an island and state on the north-west coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a>, developed by the British as a port from 1786. It became a major trading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entrepot">entrepôt</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strait-of-malacca">Strait of Malacca</a>. The site's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya Empire</a> profile places it in a line of entrepôts, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>, that followed the commercial model established by Srivijaya.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/penang.jpg" alt="Penang" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original designer of the flag is unknown. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Penang_(Malaysia).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
